---
/**
 * /faq — ALL FOURTEEN QUESTIONS, GROUPED. The page spec §3.2 describes in
 * one line: "All 14 of §37's questions, grouped: Cost & Pricing / Helpers
 * & Sources / Process & Timing / Replacement."
 *
 * THREE BLOCKS, AND THE MIDDLE ONE IS THE PAGE. Unlike the four Phase B
 * pages before it, this page has almost no prose of its own: the content
 * is the collection, and every sentence in it has already been reviewed
 * and shipped. What this file owns is the frame — a short hero that says
 * what the list is and links the other two corners of the triangle, the
 * grouped list, and the CTA.
 *
 * SPEC §4 GIVES THIS PAGE THE LONG-TAIL INTENT, "via FAQPage structured
 * data across all 14". That is the page's actual SEO mechanism, and it is
 * why <Faq /> is deliberately NOT rendered here. Faq.astro emits its own
 * FAQPage block whenever `emitSchema` is left at its default; rendering
 * both components would put two FAQPage blocks on one page, which is a
 * structured-data defect rather than twice the signal. FaqGrouped emits
 * the single block covering every entry.
 *
 * THE INTERNAL LINKING TRIANGLE (spec §4) CLOSES HERE. Pricing ↔ Find Your
 * Helper ↔ FAQ was unbuildable in sub-project 1 because there was nowhere
 * to link. The FAQ entries themselves already link to /pricing — several
 * of them — but they may not link to /find-your-helper: tests/content.test.ts
 * forbids any file under src/content from doing so, because a markdown body
 * is shared across surfaces and cannot know which page it is on. So the
 * third edge is drawn here, in the page file, where it can be.
 *
 * NO INLINE CTA PAIR, for /about's reason: FinalCta sits directly under
 * the last group, and a second pair of buttons a few hundred pixels above
 * it would put two conversion surfaces in one screen. The mobile CTA bar
 * is fixed on every page regardless.
 *
 * NO FREQUENCY CLAIM ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE. "The questions we're asked
 * most often" ranks questions by how often they arrive and nobody has that
 * data — the defect W-6 deleted from /pricing twice and Faq.astro's own
 * default lede a third time. This page states what the list IS (all of
 * them, grouped by subject), which is a fact about the page rather than a
 * claim about DirectHired's phone calls. Spec §2.6.4 records the one thing
 * DirectHired did say about what families ask — that they re-ask for
 * reassurance — and that is not a ranking.
 *
 * GROUNDS: cream / white / cream, registered in
 * tests/section-rhythm.test.ts. FinalCta is fixed at --color-surface
 * because the homepage renders the same component, which fixes the middle
 * block white; opening on cream is what all four earlier pages do.
 *
 * NO BRAND WASH, and it is a decision rather than an omission. The
 * register's rule is "at most one" --color-surface-teal section per page,
 * and this page spends none. There are only two candidates: the hero,
 * which would make /faq the one page on the site that does not open on the
 * page ground, and the list, which would put the brand wash behind ~1,400px
 * of collapsed accordion rows — the definition of wallpaper that
 * tests/section-rhythm.test.ts's own comment warns about. Neither earns
 * it. Stated so that adding one is a decision somebody takes rather than a
 * background flipped in this file.
 *
 * NO SECOND DARK BAND — TwoSidedMatch is not rendered here (spec §3.2 does
 * not list it for this page), so block 07 remains the site's only
 * --color-deep section.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Container from '../components/Container.astro'
import FaqGrouped from '../sections/FaqGrouped.astro'
import FinalCta from '../sections/FinalCta.astro'

/*
 * Long tail (spec §4), so the title names the SUBJECTS rather than a
 * single query: the four groups are what the fourteen questions are about,
 * and they are also what somebody types. No figure and no licence number
 * here — /pricing owns the figures in its title and /about owns the
 * licence, and both are single-sourced there.
 */
const title = 'Domestic Helper FAQs — Cost, Sources, Process, Replacement | DirectHired'
const description =
  'Answers about hiring a domestic helper in Singapore: what the fly-in package covers, ' +
  'where DirectHired’s helpers come from, how long a placement takes, and how the 6-month ' +
  'replacement works.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} breadcrumb="FAQ">
  <section class="faq-intro">
    <Container>
      {/*
        The <h1> is a statement about the page, not about the questions.
        "Every question we answer" is true and checkable — FaqGrouped
        renders the whole collection and fails the build rather than
        dropping an entry — where "the questions families ask most" would
        be a claim about data nobody has.
      */}
      <h1>Every question we answer, in one place.</h1>

      <p class="faq-lede">
        Cost and pricing, where our helpers come from, how a placement runs, and how replacement
        works. Open any question to read the answer.
      </p>

      {/*
        The third edge of spec §4's triangle. Both links point at pages
        that go further than an FAQ answer can, which is also why they are
        worth a visitor's click rather than being link decoration.
      */}
      <p class="faq-body">
        Two of these subjects have a page of their own: every figure is itemised on
        <a href="/pricing">pricing</a>, and the matching is explained step by step on
        <a href="/find-your-helper">find your helper</a>.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <FaqGrouped />

  {/*
    Framed for this page: a visitor who has read fourteen answers has read
    everything this site can tell them in general, and the next thing is
    the part that is specific to their household. "A consultant reads every
    submission" is already published site copy (master brief line 353's
    intake role, which faq/submit-requirements.md states) and deliberately
    stops short of a response time, which that entry owns and states as
    within 1 business day.
  */}
  <FinalCta
    heading="Still a question this page does not answer?"
    lede="The answers above are the general ones. Send us your household’s requirements and a consultant will come back to you about yours."
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .faq-intro {
    /*
     * --space-12 top, --space-section bottom — Hero's treatment, and the
     * treatment /pricing, /find-your-helper, /why-directhired and /about
     * all give their opening block, for the same reason: this block
     * carries the page's hero, and a full --space-section (128px at ≥1280)
     * above an image-less single-column headline spends the first screen
     * on cream.
     */
    padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--space-section);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .faq-intro h1 {
    margin: 0;
    /*
     * 18ch, the measure /pricing and /find-your-helper use. This headline
     * is a 38-character sentence; at --size-h1's 64px it breaks once,
     * after "answer", which puts "in one place." on its own line — the
     * clause that says what is different about this page.
     */
    max-width: 18ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--size-h1);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .faq-lede {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-text);
    font-size: var(--size-lede);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .faq-body {
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-text);
    font-size: var(--size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  /* --color-accent (6.03:1 on cream), never --color-brand-teal, which
     measures 2.89:1 and carries no text anywhere on this site. */
  .faq-body a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  .faq-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    border-color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>
